{# DMARC *policy* badge — what a domain asks receivers to do with mail that
   fails alignment.

   WHY this is not `<twig:StatusBadge>`: that component's colour map is keyed
   for message *disposition* (what a receiver actually did to a message), where
   `reject` means "blocked" and correctly earns a red badge. Policy runs the
   opposite way — `p=reject` is full enforcement, the strongest posture, and the
   destination the managed auto-ramp (DEC-058) drives customers toward. Sharing
   one map inverted the scale: the best outcome rendered red beside the domain
   name while the weakest, most spoofable state rendered neutral grey.

   Severity therefore ascends with protection: warning (spoofable, act) ->
   info (enforcement under way) -> success (fully enforced).

   The fallback arm is neutral on purpose. An unrecognised or absent policy is
   unknown, not broken, and CLAUDE.md requires the last arm to carry no error
   tone. #}
{% props policy, label = null %}

{% set badgeClass = {
    'none': 'badge-warning',
    'quarantine': 'badge-info',
    'reject': 'badge-success',
}[policy] ?? 'badge-ghost' %}

<span class="badge badge-sm {{ badgeClass }}">{{ label ?? policy }}</span>
